%% Kaur Khor stability benchmark architecture.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Bench as Stability benchmark<br/>tests/bench/scenarios/stability.bench.ts
  participant Shell as KaurKhorShell sidebar
  participant Router as React Router<br/>route observers
  participant Routes as Repeated route surfaces
  participant Provider as Providers and route caches
  participant Preload as Preload bridge
  participant Main as Electron main IPC
  participant Core as Managed desktop-core pool
  participant Store as SQLite read models
  participant Metrics as Benchmark summary

  Bench->>Provider: wait for renderer.workspace.ready
  Bench->>Metrics: record benchmark.phase.measurement_start

  loop four sidebar cycles
    Bench->>Shell: click Record update
    Shell->>Router: navigate /record-update
    Router->>Routes: mount route and wait route.record-update.ready
    Routes->>Provider: read route context
    Provider->>Preload: route support reads when needed
    Preload->>Main: IPC read command
    Main->>Core: cached or coalesced read
    Core->>Store: read route rows
    Store-->>Routes: route data

    Bench->>Shell: click Performance, Catalog, Financials, Automations, Analysis, Logs, Overview
    Shell->>Router: repeat route transitions
    Router->>Metrics: route.*.ready for each destination
    Bench->>Metrics: record selected nav.* duration metrics
    Bench->>Metrics: snapshot memory.renderer_stability_cycle_N_mb
  end

  Bench->>Metrics: snapshot memory.renderer_after_stability_mb
  Bench->>Metrics: record benchmark.phase.measurement_end
  Bench->>Metrics: close app and persist stability summary

  Note over Bench,Metrics: The stability routine is crash-free coverage plus memory-slope inputs, not a single latency path.
  Note over Provider,Core: Repeated route churn exercises lazy chunks, renderer caches, read coalescing, and cache invalidation boundaries.
